  "result": "{\"seen_before\": false, \"matches\": [], \"answer\": \"I found no past ticket that reports this problem. That means Quick Accent turns on Caps Lock when Keyboard Manager has Backspace and Caps Lock swapped. A few tickets are loosely related but describe different problems. PowerToys#25435 and PowerToys#1692 cover Caps Lock being toggled or showing the wrong state after a Keyboard Manager remap. Neither involves Quick Accent. Please keep this ticket open as a new bug. Add your exact remap (Backspace to Caps Lock and Caps Lock to Backspace) and the Quick Accent activation key you use. Add a PowerToys bug report ZIP too. As a workaround, you could remap only one of the two keys, or turn Quick Accent off while the swap is active.\"}",
